# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vlax-vb-constants-unbound — vlax-vbInteger, vlax-vbDouble ... are nil after (vl-load-com)
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-vlax-vb-constants-unbound
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

Found while fixing vlax-variant-type (cador-intersectwith-missing):

: (vl-load-com)
: (list vlax-vbInteger vlax-vbDouble vlax-vbString)   ; clautolisp => (nil nil nil)

The specification names them as the type arguments of vlax-make-safearray,
vlax-make-variant and vlax-variant-change-type (Function Entry:
VLAX-MAKE-SAFEARRAY: vlax-vbInteger, vlax-vbLong, vlax-vbSingle,
vlax-vbDouble, vlax-vbString, vlax-vbObject, vlax-vbBoolean, vlax-vbVariant;
VLAX-MAKE-VARIANT: "an integer defaults to vlax-vbLong"), so the canonical
=(vlax-make-safearray vlax-vbDouble '(0 . 2))= passes nil as the type.

* Cause

The ActiveX constants installed by (vl-load-com) are the GENERATED table of
probe-activex-constants.lsp (activex-constants-table.lisp), whose name list
has no vlax-vb* entry; nothing else binds them.

* Proposal

Add the vlax-vb* names (vlax-vbEmpty 0, vlax-vbNull 1, vlax-vbInteger 2,
vlax-vbLong 3, vlax-vbSingle 4, vlax-vbDouble 5, vlax-vbCurrency 6,
vlax-vbDate 7, vlax-vbString 8, vlax-vbObject 9, vlax-vbError 10,
vlax-vbBoolean 11, vlax-vbVariant 12, vlax-vbDataObject 13,
vlax-vbDecimal 14, vlax-vbByte 17, vlax-vbArray 8192 -- the VB VarType
values) to probe-activex-constants.lsp, run it on AutoCAD and BricsCAD,
regenerate the table. Since 2.3.10 vlax-make-variant /
vlax-variant-change-type / vlax-make-safearray accept the integer codes, so
binding the names is all that is missing.

* Acceptance criteria

- The measured values bound after (vl-load-com), per product.
- =(vlax-variant-type (vlax-make-variant 1 vlax-vbInteger))= = 2.

* Fix (2026-10-22)

Partial: bound from the DOCUMENTED values, the vendor measurement pending.

- probes/sources/probe-activex-constants.lsp: the 17 vlax-vb* names are
  appended to the inventory, so the next AutoCAD / BricsCAD run records
  (boundp value) for each, and the regenerated activex-constants-table.lisp
  carries them per product.
- clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp: a hand-written
  *ACTIVEX-DOCUMENTED-CONSTANTS* (NAME AUTOCAD BRICSCAD), same shape as the
  generated *ACTIVEX-MEASURED-CONSTANTS*, kept OUT of the generated file so a
  regeneration cannot clobber it. INSTALL-ACTIVEX-ENUMERATION-CONSTANTS
  installs ACTIVEX-DOCUMENTED-CONSTANTS after the measured ones, same rules
  (per product, once per document, never over a non-nil value), and a name
  the measured table records is skipped: the measurement wins, even a
  product's NIL. Once the measured table has all 17, the documented table
  can be deleted.
- Spec: a "*** clautolisp" note on VLAX-MAKE-SAFEARRAY.
- Tests (autolisp-builtins-core): vlax-vb-constants-bound-after-vl-load-com,
  vlax-vb-constants-yield-to-the-measured-table,
  vlax-vb-constants-drive-make-variant-and-safearray --
  (vlax-variant-type (vlax-make-variant 1 vlax-vbInteger)) = 2.

Remaining: run probe-activex-constants on AutoCAD and BricsCAD, regenerate
the table, check the values against the documented ones.

* Measured (2026-10-23)

probe-activex-constants.lsp, inventory cases, (boundp value) after
(vl-load-com): AutoCAD 2022 Windows (run 20261023T074943Z), BricsCAD V25
Windows (20261023T075150Z), BricsCAD V26 macOS (20261023T031215Z). Both
BricsCAD builds agree.

| name              | documented | AutoCAD 2022 | BricsCAD V25 / V26 |
|-------------------+------------+--------------+--------------------|
| vlax-vbEmpty      |          0 |            0 |                  0 |
| vlax-vbNull       |          1 |            1 |                  1 |
| vlax-vbInteger    |          2 |            2 |                  2 |
| vlax-vbLong       |          3 |            3 |                  3 |
| vlax-vbSingle     |          4 |            4 |                  4 |
| vlax-vbDouble     |          5 |            5 |                  5 |
| vlax-vbCurrency   |          6 |            6 |                  6 |
| vlax-vbDate       |          7 |            7 |                  7 |
| vlax-vbString     |          8 |            8 |                  8 |
| vlax-vbObject     |          9 |            9 |                  9 |
| vlax-vbError      |         10 |           10 |                 10 |
| vlax-vbBoolean    |         11 |           11 |                 11 |
| vlax-vbVariant    |         12 |           12 |                 12 |
| vlax-vbDataObject |         13 |           13 |                 13 |
| vlax-vbDecimal    |         14 |          nil |                 14 |
| vlax-vbByte       |         17 |          nil |                nil |
| vlax-vbArray      |       8192 |         8192 |               8192 |

nil: not bound. Every bound value is the documented one; vlax-vbDecimal is BricsCAD-only and
vlax-vbByte is bound by neither product.

(Side observation: on AutoCAD the case names of the bound ones read back in
mixed case -- vl-symbol-name of 'vlax-vbempty is "vlax-vbEmpty" -- while the
unbound ones are upper case: AutoCAD keeps the case of the name its own
code interned the symbol with. Same phenomenon as
type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad; not implemented here.)

Implemented (2026-10-23):

- clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/activex-constants-table.lisp:
  the 16 names bound by at least one product added to
  *ACTIVEX-MEASURED-CONSTANTS* by hand, in the generator's format and
  order ((NAME AUTOCAD BRICSCAD), sorted, NIL for "not bound"; a name
  bound by neither -- vlax-vbByte -- has no entry), header updated
  (951 names measured, 847 bound on AutoCAD, 948 on BricsCAD).
- clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp: the hand-written
  *ACTIVEX-DOCUMENTED-CONSTANTS* and ACTIVEX-DOCUMENTED-CONSTANTS deleted
  (redundant: everything is measured); the installer binds the measured
  table only. So: AutoCAD dialects 15 names (no vlax-vbDecimal, no
  vlax-vbByte), BricsCAD dialects 16 (no vlax-vbByte), strict the 15
  common ones, clautolisp / lax 16. The integer code 17 is still accepted
  by vlax-make-variant & co.
- Spec: the "*** clautolisp" note on VLAX-MAKE-SAFEARRAY now gives the
  measured values.
- Tests: vlax-vb-constants-bound-after-vl-load-com (per dialect, measured
  values), vlax-vb-constants-yield-to-the-measured-table (now: no
  documented table, the measured one carries them per product),
  vlax-vb-constants-drive-make-variant-and-safearray (unchanged),
  activex-constants-every-measured-constant-bound-per-product (847 / 948).
